# AI dev workflow

Canonical: `docs/AI_DEV_WORKFLOW.md`

## Loop (one goal = one branch)

0. Split/design goal + AC (`docs/work/<goal-id>.md`) — **no code yet**
1. Branch from trunk: `feat|fix|docs|chore|rea/<goal-id>-<short>`
2. Implement + `DOC_SYNC`
3. Verify AC
4. Run tests
5. Code review (constraints, layout, secrets)
6. Gap check — must-fix in-scope only; else backlog
7. Commit only if DoD pass **and** user/automation allowed commit
8. Push (no force to main)
9. Merge to trunk via PR when possible
10. Return to trunk; mark goal done

## Hard stops

- Do not commit/push/merge if AC, tests, review, or DOC_SYNC fail.
- Do not expand scope mid-branch; spawn a new Goal ID.
- Do not commit directly to `main` by default.
- Never commit `.local/`, weights, secrets.

## DoD

AC ✅ + tests ✅ + review ✅ + DOC_SYNC ✅ + gitignore clean + Goal ID in commit message.
